  the wide-ranging influences of his five-decade career\, Don Was brings hi
 s Pan-Detroit Ensemble to the stage to celebrate the 50th anniversary of t
 he Grateful Dead’s landmark album Terrapin Station\, presenting the albu
 m in its entirety. Building on Don’s long musical association with Bobby
  Weir\, the Ensemble brings its own musical personality to the Dead’s mu
 sic\, offering a fresh interpretation through its distinctive blend of ste
 amy jazz\, juke-joint blues\, and loose-limbed funk. The concert will also
  feature music from the band’s debut album\, Groove in the Face of Adver
 sity\, which channels the soul of the Motor City through a sound both time
